                <h2>Expert Dermatologic Surgery</h2>
                <p>Our board-certified dermatologists have extensive training and experience in dermatologic surgery. We perform a wide range of surgical procedures to remove skin cancers, benign growths, and other skin lesions with precision and care.</p>
                
                <h3>Surgical Procedures We Offer</h3>
                
                <h4>Skin Cancer Treatment</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Surgical Excision</strong> – Complete removal of skin cancer with clear margins</li>
                    <li><strong>Electrodesiccation & Curettage</strong> – For superficial skin cancers</li>
                    <li><strong>Mohs Surgery Referrals</strong> – We coordinate care with Mohs surgeons for complex cases</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h4>Mole & Lesion Removal</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Mole Removal</strong> – Suspicious or cosmetically concerning moles</li>
                    <li><strong>Skin Tag Removal</strong> – Quick, simple removal</li>
                    <li><strong>Lipoma Excision</strong> – Removal of benign fatty tumors</li>
                    <li><strong>Benign Tumor Removal</strong> – Seborrheic keratoses, dermatofibromas, etc.</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h4>Cyst Treatment</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Cyst Excision</strong> – Complete removal of epidermoid and pilar cysts</li>
                    <li><strong>Cyst Drainage</strong> – For infected or inflamed cysts</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h4>Other Procedures</h4>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Skin Biopsies</strong> – Diagnostic sampling for pathology analysis</li>
                    <li><strong>Ingrown Toenail Surgery</strong> – Permanent correction</li>
                    <li><strong>Scar Revision</strong> – Improving the appearance of scars</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>What to Expect</h3>
                <p>Most dermatologic surgeries are performed in our office under local anesthesia. Here's what you can typically expect:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>The area is numbed with local anesthetic – you'll feel pressure but no pain</li>
                    <li>The procedure usually takes 15-45 minutes depending on complexity</li>
                    <li>Sutures may be placed and removed 1-2 weeks later</li>
                    <li>You'll receive detailed wound care instructions</li>
                    <li>Most patients return to normal activities the same day</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Our Commitment to Excellence</h3>
                <p>We prioritize both complete removal and optimal cosmetic outcomes. Our surgeons use meticulous technique and careful closure to minimize scarring while ensuring complete treatment of the condition.</p>
